# 19. Full Fine-Tuning Experiment

After understanding LoRA, optionally try full fine-tuning.

Conceptually:

```text
LoRA:

600M base parameters
       ↓
mostly frozen
       ↓
small adapter trained


Full fine-tuning:

600M base parameters
       ↓
all parameters updated
```

Full fine-tuning is useful educationally because you can understand the difference between:

```text
trainable parameters
```

and:

```text
total parameters
```

However, do not start with a large dataset or long context.

